  "name": null,
  "problem": "A local newspaper is sold by three distributors, $1,$ $2,$ and $3.$\n\n- Distributor $1$ buys $33%$ of the copies, and $90%$ of those copies are sold.\n\n- Distributor $2$ buys $25%$ of the copies, and $87%$ of those copies are sold.\n\n- Distributor $3$ buys $42%$ of the copies, and $82%$ of those copies are sold.\n\nIf $5%$ of all copies have some printing defect, and $70%$ of defective copies are sold, what is the probability that a randomly chosen sold copy has a printing defect? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
